{
  "version": 1,
  "scalar_models": {
    "lean": "Exact algebra over CommRing, with real-number theorems where required",
    "cpp": "C++20 operations over IEEE-754 binary32 or binary64",
    "esbmc": "Quaternion/SO(3): binary32 except Q-ROT-MATRIX/Q-ROTATE, which also have binary64 profiles in formal/cpp/esbmc/rotation.cpp. Rotation actions use an opaque matrix-producer summary with separate actual-producer row proofs and an actual-backend basis lemma; no matrix value constraints are assumed by the action proof. E-STATE/E-PRED: separate binary32 and binary64 profiles, both ESKF_QUAT_APPROX modes and both alias cases. Per-entry domains and fixtures remain explicit; proof-backend results do not verify Eigen or PX4 internals."
  },
  "review_dimensions": [
    "coefficient ordering",
    "Hamilton multiplication and composition order",
    "active rotation and column-vector convention",
    "preconditions and valid domains",
    "coefficient-level equations and evaluation order",
    "postconditions and failure behavior",
    "exact algebra versus IEEE-754 claims",
    "ESBMC assumptions and vacuity risk"
  ],
